# Raw client material — §7z-C keeps this in the local-only column.
#
# raw/ IS NOW IGNORED WHOLESALE (2026-09-22). It used to be an enumerated blocklist:
# every raw/<client-work>/ folder listed by hand at intake. That design fails open —
# the cost of forgetting a line, or mistyping one, is a client's material sitting
# unignored in a public repo, and both have happened. raw/model-video-09-05/ was a
# path that did not exist on disk and so matched nothing for 8 days, and the 682 MB
# of client-009 craft material in raw/year-of-goat-09-10/ was never listed at all;
# it was recorded as an exposure three times (client-008, lead-003, client-009)
# before being moved out of this repo entirely on 2026-09-22.
#
# A blocklist has to be right every time. This rule has to be right once.
#
# The 33 files already tracked under raw/ are UNAFFECTED — .gitignore does not untrack
# anything, and those are our own GSC exports, SEO audits and spec notes, deliberately
# committed. They stay tracked and their edits still show up in git status.
# To commit something new under raw/ on purpose, `git add -f` it, and be sure first.
raw/

# The per-folder lines below are now redundant and are KEPT ON PURPOSE. Each carries
# the note explaining what is in that folder and why it may not be published, which is
# worth more than the line itself; and if anyone ever narrows the raw/ rule above with
# a `!` exception, these still hold the client folders shut.
raw/context-enrichment-08-31/
raw/cute-city-08-25/
raw/agent-skills-08-31/
raw/studio-retouching-09-02/
raw/retouching-09-01/
# SEMrush bulk keyword export for the retouching-buyer terms (action #6 of the
# 09-15 demand doc). The screenshot is the only copy, so the numbers are
# transcribed into docs/workstream-seo-smm-growth.md § 2026-09-15 — same handling
# as raw/agent-skills-08-31/ and raw/retouching-09-01/ above.
raw/photo-retouching-seo-09-15/
# OOTD video client material: a real woman's reference video (no release) + the client's
# lookbook photo. Was listed as `raw/model-video-09-05/` from 2026-09-07 — a path that does
# not exist on disk, so the line matched nothing and the real folder sat unignored in this
# public repo for 8 days (never committed). Corrected 2026-09-15; verify any new line here
# with `git check-ignore -v <path>`. §7z record: client-006 ootd-video, round 7.
raw/fashion-model-09-05/

